{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2-repair-001\\\\specs\\\\R4_WO-SWOF-W2-R004_SPEC.md' -Raw | Out-String -Width 200\"","aggregated_output":"# R4 WO-SWOF-W2-R004 — canonical HumanGate trigger, ruin precedence, and exact ApprovalToken integrity\n\nrepair_id: SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R2\norder_id: SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R2\nbase: the R3 candidate (see the writer prompt for the exact SHA)\nsource: the two external challenge reports (W2R1-EXT-001..004) — findings the repair MUST close\n\n## 0. Confirmed defects this round must close\n\n```\nD1 BLOCKING  P3/P4/P5 + benign operation name + no token -> ALLOWED.\n             PI06 TOK-INV-001 is RISK-TIER based: \"P3/P4/P5 without valid exact Human token ->\n             DENY_P3_TOKEN_REQUIRED\". The operation name may TIGHTEN or identify the route; it may\n             never WEAKEN a risk/permission requirement. An in-repo test cannot redefine the predicate.\nD2 BLOCKING  RUIN / UNKNOWN_RUIN are not implemented at all: a valid token must NOT authorize RUIN.\nD3 BLOCKING  ApprovalToken integrity/lineage/basis is under-bound:\n             - canonical payload is plain sorted JSON, NOT RFC 8785 JCS;\n             - the required fixed domain frame is missing;\n             - signature verification receives the wrong bytes;\n             - approval_basis_hash is only shape-checked, never recomputed;\n             - no request->decision->token lineage (request_id / decision_id);\n             - consumer audience is optional when ctx lacks an expected hash;\n             - generations only fail when the caller happens to supply one.\n```\n\n## 1. Files you may write (exactly these, nothing else)\n\n```\nsrc/security/humangate.py                          (modify)\nsrc/security/rights.py                             (modify: unify the gate predicate + ruin precedence)\nsrc/security/tests/test_humangate_currentness.py   (modify: add the cases in section 6)\nsrc/security/tests/test_rights.py                  (modify)\nschemas/security/approval_token.schema.json        (modify only if canonical requires)\n```\n\nASCII only. LF line endings. You MAY import `cryptography` (present in this environment) for Ed25519\nONLY. No other new dependency. No network.\n\n## 2. D1 + D2 — ONE canonical gate predicate, ruin before approval\n\nIn `rights.py`, replace the two drifting gates with ONE predicate used by every caller:\n\n```python\ndef human_gate_required(request) -> HumanGateRoute:\n    \"\"\"ONE canonical gate predicate. Risk/permission classification is authoritative; the operation\n    name may TIGHTEN the route (identify its authority edge) but may NEVER weaken it.\"\"\"\n```\n\nRules, in this order:\n\n```\n1. ruin precedence FIRST, before any approval consideration:\n     request.ruin_class == \"RUIN\"          -> HumanGateRoute(required=True, route=RUIN_HARD_VETO_ROUTE,\n                                                            authority_edge=\"RUIN:HARD_VETO\")\n     request.ruin_class == \"UNKNOWN_RUIN\"  -> HumanGateRoute(required=True, route=RUIN_SAFE_STOP_ROUTE,\n                                                            authority_edge=\"RUIN:SAFE_STOP\")\n     (a token can never satisfy these; the verifier must reject them BEFORE checking approval)\n2. token required if ANY of:\n     request.effect_risk_tier in {\"P3\",\"P4\",\"P5\"}\n     request.permission_class in {\"P3\",\"P4\",\"P5\"}\n     the operation maps to an explicit high-risk authority edge (existing HIGH_RISK_ACTIONS)\n   -> HumanGateRoute(required=True, route=HUMAN_GATE_ROUTE, authority_edge=<edge or \"HUMAN_GATE:risk_tier\">)\n3. otherwise -> HumanGateRoute(required=False, route=NONE_ROUTE, authority_edge=\"NONE\")\n```\n\n`assert_human_gate_satisfied(route, approval, *, requesting_actor=None, request=None, ctx=None)` must:\n\n- keep `UNKNOWN_ROUTE_FAIL_CLOSED` for a non-route;\n- RE-DERIVE the route from `request` when a request is supplied and refuse if the passed route\n  understates it (`ROUTE_UNDERSTATES_ACTION`) — keep the existing behaviour;\n- for a RUIN / UNKNOWN_RUIN route raise `HumanGateBypassAttempt(\"HARD_VETO_RUIN\")` /\n  `HumanGateBypassAttempt(\"SAFE_STOP_UNKNOWN_RUIN\")` **regardless of the token**, before any token check;\n- for a P3/P4/P5 request with a non-token approval raise `DENY_P3_TOKEN_REQUIRED` (keep);\n- a `required=False` route reached with `request=None` still raises `ROUTE_NOT_REDERIVABLE_FAIL_CLOSED`.\n\nAdd `ruin_class: str = \"NONE\"` to `ApprovalRequest` (values `NONE | RUIN | UNKNOWN_RUIN`).\n\n## 3. D3 — canonical integrity, basis and lineage\n\n### 3.1 RFC 8785 JCS (implement it EXACTLY, do not approximate)\n\nAdd `jcs_dumps(obj) -> bytes` implementing RFC 8785:\n- object keys sorted by UTF-16 code units;\n- strings escaped per the JCS/JSON rules with no unnecessary escapes, output as UTF-8;\n- numbers serialized per ECMAScript `Number::toString` (integers without `.0`; no `+`; no exponent for\n  the range JCS requires) — implement a correct integer/decimal path and, for anything outside the\n  range you can prove, RAISE rather than emit a wrong form;\n- `true`/`false`/`null` literals; arrays in order; no insignificant whitespace.\nInclude a docstring stating the profile is `RFC8785` and that it is NOT `json.dumps(sort_keys=True)`.\nAdd `tests` proving: key ordering by UTF-16, no-spaces output, integer `1` not `1.0`, and a\nnon-ASCII string round-trip.\n\n### 3.2 Domain framing\n\n```python\nDOMAIN_FRAME = b\"SWOF:PI-PKG-06:DOC-03:APPROVAL-TOKEN:V1\\x00\"\n\ndef canonical_payload_bytes(token) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"JCS(token without `signature`), prefixed with DOMAIN_FRAME. These are the exact bytes a\n    verifier signs/verifies.\"\"\"\n    body = {k: v for k, v in asdict(token).items() if k != \"signature\"}\n    return DOMAIN_FRAME + jcs_dumps(body)\n```\n\nKeep the function name and semantics: the registry verifier receives exactly these bytes.\n\n### 3.3 Qualified Ed25519 verification\n\n`VerificationContext.trusted_key_registry` becomes a **key resolver**: call it as\n`registry(issuer_id, key_id, key_generation)` and it must return the Ed25519 public key as `bytes`\n(32) or a `cryptography` public-key object; anything else, `None`, an exception, or a callable that\ncannot supply a key must FAIL CLOSED with `DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY`.\n\nThen verify with `cryptography`:\n\n```python\nEd25519PublicKey.from_public_bytes(key_bytes).verify(signature_b64url_decoded, canonical_payload_bytes(token))\n```\n\n- signature must be base64url WITHOUT padding decoding to exactly 64 bytes; otherwise `DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY`;\n- `InvalidSignature` -> `DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY`;\n- document that this is a REAL Ed25519 verification over the RFC8785-framed bytes, not a shape check.\n\n### 3.4 Lineage and basis\n\n- add `request_id` and `decision_id` to `ApprovalRequest` and to the token (they are already canonical\n  token fields);\n- the verifier must require `token.request_id == request.request_id` and\n  `token.decision_id == request.decision_id`; mismatch -> `DENY_EXACT_BINDING`;\n- add `decision_basis_hash` and `generation_bundle_digest` and `rollback_digest` to `ApprovalRequest`;\n- compute the expected basis exactly as PI06 §15.5 requires and compare:\n\n```python\ndef approval_basis_hash(decision_basis_hash, effect_digest, generation_bundle_digest,\n                        rollback_digest, consumer_audience_hash, if06b_version) -> str:\n    \"\"\"SHA-256 hex of b\"SWOF-D03-APPROVAL-BASIS-V1\\\\n\" || the six fields joined in that exact order.\"\"\"\n```\n\n  mismatch -> `DENY_APPROVAL_BASIS` (new code, add it to the documented set).\n\n### 3.5 Audience, generations, checker flag — all mandatory where canonical says so\n\n- a gated route requires `ctx.expected_consumer_audience_hash`; if it is `None`/malformed -> `DENY_AUDIENCE_MISMATCH`;\n- the generation set the request declares must be present in `ctx` and equal the token's: if the\n  request declares a generation and `ctx` lacks it -> `DENY_STALE_GENERATION` (no silent skip);\n- `token.independent_checker_required is True` requires a non-empty\n  `ctx.independent_checker_evidence_ref` AND equality with the token's — **whenever it is true**,\n  not only for T3; T3 additionally forces `independent_checker_required` to be true\n  (`DENY_T3_CHECKER` if false).\n\n### 3.6 Version syntax tightening (opportunistic, same file)\n\n`if06b_version`, `payload_schema_version`, `min_reader_version` must match `^\\d+\\.\\d+$` (and\n`^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$` for `payload_schema_version`) exactly — reject `\"1\"` and `\"1.0.0.0\"` with\n`DENY_TOKEN_SCHEMA` / `IF06B_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED` as today.\n\n## 4. Keep everything already proven\n\nDo not weaken or remove: currentness fail-closed in `rights.py`; credential-scope expiry; typed-token\nrequirement for bare strings; exact binding on subject/hash/op/target/resource/scope/environment/\npurpose/data_class/effect_digest/consumer_audience_hash; token time window (equality at expiry\ninvalid); token state; approver != actor; false-authority prefixes; nonce consume-once; rollback for\nP3+; T3 checker; the 42 required schema fields (set-equal, verify the count yourself and state it).\n\n## 5. Absolute rules\n\n- Fail closed. No wall clock reads. No approximate JCS. No fake crypto.\n- One gate predicate, one authority path; do not add a second router or authority system.\n\n## 6. Tests you MUST add (acceptance evidence)\n\n```\nD1   P3 + operation \"read\" + no token            -> DENY_P3_TOKEN_REQUIRED\nD1   P4 + operation \"read\" + no token            -> DENY_P3_TOKEN_REQUIRED\nD1   P5 + operation \"read\" + no token            -> DENY_P3_TOKEN_REQUIRED\nD1   P3 (permission_class only) + benign op      -> DENY_P3_TOKEN_REQUIRED\nD1   P3 + benign op + valid exact token          -> PASS\nD1   P2 + benign op + no token                   -> allowed (positive control)\nD1   explicit high-risk operation + P2 + no token-> gated\nD2   valid exact token + ruin_class RUIN         -> HARD_VETO_RUIN (token cannot override)\nD2   valid exact token + ruin_class UNKNOWN_RUIN -> SAFE_STOP_UNKNOWN_RUIN\nD2   no token + RUIN                             -> HARD_VETO_RUIN\nD3   signature over NON-framed payload           -> DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY\nD3   signature over framed but non-JCS payload   -> DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY\nD3   wrong key_generation / unknown key          -> DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY\nD3   registry returns bytes key + CORRECT signature -> PASS (positive control through real Ed25519)\nD3   wrong request_id / decision_id              -> DENY_EXACT_BINDING\nD3   wrong approval_basis_hash                   -> DENY_APPROVAL_BASIS\nD3   request declares a generation ctx lacks     -> DENY_STALE_GENERATION\nD3   gated request with expected audience None   -> DENY_AUDIENCE_MISMATCH\nD3   checker_required=true + missing checker ref -> (canonical code)\nD3   T3 + checker_required=false                 -> DENY_T3_CHECKER\nJCS  key ordering by UTF-16; no whitespace; integer not float; non-ASCII round-trip\n```\nEvery previously passing test must still pass; the denominator may only grow.\n\n## 7. When finished print exactly one JSON object\n\n```json\n{\"files\": [\"<every path you wrote>\"], \"test_command\": \"<the command you ran>\",\n \"test_result\": \"<stdout tail>\", \"denominator\": <int tests collected in src/security/tests>,\n \"schema_required_count\": <int>}\n```\n\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
