{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_90","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$f='\"'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\知識庫\\\\實作相關DOC\\\\Fabric vNext\\\\Semantic World OS Fabric\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_Pre-Dev_Multi-Packages\\\\PI-PKG\\\\DOC\\\\PI-PKG-06_DOC\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_PI-PKG-06_DOC-03_2026-09-10_r2_FULL_REPAIR.md'; Get-Content -LiteralPath \"'$f | Select-Object -Skip 425 -First 75 | Out-String -Width 200'","aggregated_output":"| merge | repo/ref/commit digest | P5 + explicit Human + checker |\r\n| deploy/release | artifact/env/version | P5 + explicit Human + checker |\r\n| financial effect | amount/currency/account purpose | P3 minimum; T3 by materiality/domain |\r\n| physical actuation | device/capability/safety envelope | T3 unless domain proves lower bounded class |\r\n| irreversible deletion | exact resource + irreversibility | T3; RUIN/UNKNOWN_RUIN veto/safe-stop |\r\n\r\n## 09.R｜Retained r1 details under r2 closure\r\n\r\nThis is a **first-class parent-projected responsibility surface**. DOC-03 r2 contract explicitly separates two axes that r1 partially conflated:\r\n\r\n- `SubjectRiskClass`: what risk/ruin condition exists in the **subject/domain/resource being examined**.\r\n- `EffectRiskTier`: downside/tail/irreversibility of the **pending action/effect actually being authorized**.\r\n\r\n`RuinHardVeto` attaches to a proposed consequential **effect/promotion edge**, not to the mere fact that a subject contains ruin-class information. Safe P0 diagnostic read and bounded P1 remediation design may remain admissible under rights/security/isolation policy even when the subject describes a ruin incident; they must not themselves trigger or widen the ruinous effect.\r\n\r\n| EffectRiskTier | Canonical meaning | HumanGate consequence |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| LOW | bounded, observable, reversible effect; no material external/rights/secret/financial/physical downside | P3+ still requires Human token by permission floor |\r\n| MEDIUM | limited external/business effect with reliable rollback/readback; no ruin signature | P3 hard binding; HA1/HA2 according deterministic authority matrix |\r\n| HIGH | sensitive data, material external state, identity/rights, payment, large user impact or difficult recovery | Human approval + stronger authn; domain coapproval where mapped |\r\n| CRITICAL | release, privilege/secret, irreversible deletion, large blast radius, safety-sensitive/financial/physical effect | HA1 + required HA3/HA5; AAC3 authn; safe-stop on ambiguity |\r\n| RUIN | absorbing/irreversible catastrophic or existential effect; non-offsettable | ordinary approval forbidden; `HARD_VETO`; redesign only |\r\n| UNKNOWN_RUIN | material irreversible effect downside cannot be bounded/classified | `TEMP_CLOSED / SAFE_STOP`; evidence and bounded reclassification required |\r\n\r\n## 09.1 ACTION_EFFECT_CLASS_MATRIX\r\n\r\n| Action class | Effect | Permission | Effect-risk floor | Human token | Rollback/readback floor |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| ACT-READ-LOCAL | local diagnostic/read/query; no external effect | P0 | LOW | policy rule only | read receipt/provenance when material |\r\n| ACT-DESIGN-WRITE | local design/remediation artifact only | P1 | LOW–MEDIUM | deterministic policy rule | preimage + file readback |\r\n| ACT-EXTERNAL-READ | external resource read | P2 | LOW–HIGH | policy/domain rule; rights mandatory | query receipt + provenance |\r\n| ACT-EXTERNAL-WRITE-REV | reversible external write | P3 | MEDIUM+ | YES | rollback_ref + readback |\r\n| ACT-EXTERNAL-WRITE-STATEFUL | stateful external mutation | P3 | HIGH+ | YES | rollback + EffectAttempt/reconciliation |\r\n| ACT-DATA-EXPORT | data crosses trust boundary | P3/P4 | HIGH–CRITICAL | YES | purpose/data_class/destination/revoke/readback |\r\n| ACT-SECRET-RESOLVE | access/use secret credential | P4 | CRITICAL | YES + HA3 security/privacy coapproval | scoped SecretRef only; no raw secret evidence |\r\n| ACT-IDENTITY-RIGHTS | change identity/permission/entitlement/consent | P3/P5 | CRITICAL | YES + rights/security coapproval | post-commit rights readback + rollback |\r\n| ACT-MERGE | merge protected code/config | P5 | HIGH–CRITICAL | YES | revert ref + commit readback |\r\n| ACT-DEPLOY-RELEASE | deploy/release/promote | P5 | CRITICAL | YES + HA5; release truth remains downstream | deployment readback + rollback evidence |\r\n| ACT-FINANCIAL | payment/monetary commitment | P3/P5 | HIGH–CRITICAL | YES + HA3 financial | idempotency + ledger reconciliation |\r\n| ACT-PHYSICAL | robot/OEM actuation | P3/P5 | HIGH–RUIN | YES + HA3 physical safety; HA4 veto | kill/stop + bounded world readback |\r\n| ACT-DELETE-IRREV | irreversible destruction/deletion | P3/P5 | CRITICAL–RUIN | YES if non-ruin; never overrides ruin | restore proof or HARD_VETO |\r\n\r\n## 09.2 SUBJECT_RISK_VS_EFFECT_RISK_MATRIX\r\n\r\n| Subject/domain condition | Pending action | Effect risk | Default result |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| RUIN_CLASS subject | P0 bounded diagnostic read | LOW/MEDIUM | allowed only if rights/security/isolation policy allows; no ruinous effect triggered |\r\n| RUIN_CLASS subject | P1 bounded remediation design | LOW/MEDIUM | allowed local design; cannot execute remediation effect without new classification |\r\n| UNKNOWN_RUIN subject | P0/P1 evidence gathering/design | LOW/MEDIUM | allowed only to reduce uncertainty under safe containment |\r\n| any subject | P2 external read with no effect expansion | classify actual read/privacy exposure | policy + rights; not automatically hard-vetoed by subject label |\r\n| any subject | proposed consequential effect classified RUIN | RUIN | `HARD_VETO` regardless of Human token |\r\n| any subject | material irreversible effect classification unknown | UNKNOWN_RUIN | `TEMP_CLOSED / SAFE_STOP` |\r\n# 10｜RiskTier × PermissionClass Model / Deterministic Authority Binding\r\n\r\n## 10.A Q08 RATIFIED AutonomyTier — independent axis, not an alias\r\n\r\n`AutonomyTier` is preserved exactly as an independent governance axis:\r\n\r\n| Tier | Meaning | Execution floor |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `T0` | read-only / local reversible work | MAY auto only when permission/domain/rights permit and no consequential external effect exists |\r\n| `T1` | bounded local mutation | MAY use narrow signed pre-grant (`DelegationGrant`) with exact scope, expiry, revocation and audit; it never satisfies a P3/P4/P5 floor |\r\n| `T2` | meaningful external, sensitive, financial or identity effect | MUST default to HumanGate; a standing grant is allowed only for a narrow, explicitly policy-authorized non-P3 case and never widens rights |\r\n| `T3` | ruin-bearing potential, constitutional, irreversible, high-impact rights, destructive, merge/deploy/release authority | MUST have explicit Human decision **and** independent-checker evidence before commit; if actual `EffectRiskTier=RUIN`, Human/checker cannot override the hard veto |\r\n\r\n`UNKNOWN_RUIN` never becomes T3-approvable; it becomes `SAFE_STOP` until uncertainty is reduced.\r\n\r\n## 10.B AUTONOMY_PERMISSION_RISK_AUTHORITY_MATRIX\r\n\r\n| Autonomy | Typical Permission | Effect-risk envelope | HumanGate | Independent checker | Allowed grant |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| T0 | P0/P1 | LOW–MEDIUM reversible | not required by Profile; domain may tighten | no | none |\r\n| T1 | P1 only | LOW–MEDIUM, local and bounded | pre-grant may substitute per `HG-RULE-T1-PREGRANT-001` | no | narrow `DelegationGrant`; consume/audit by operation |\r\n| T2 | P2/P3/P4 | MEDIUM–CRITICAL | default required; **P3/P4 always exact Human token** | domain-dependent unless promoted to T3 | standing grant only for explicit P2/non-P3 rule |\r\n| T3 | P3/P4/P5 | CRITICAL / irreversible / high-impact; RUIN is vetoed | explicit Human required | **required** | no standing grant; exact decision/token only |\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
